# Story 24: Resizing Panes (40s)
# Hook: Give the important pane more room -- arrow keys in layout mode flex the space.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-024-resizing-panes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Give the important pane more room -- arrow keys in layout mode flex the space.

[00:04.0 --> 00:14.0]
Start rysh, split right for a second column, then split down so we can resize in both directions.

[00:14.0 --> 00:19.0]
Press Ctrl+L. Now the arrow keys resize the active pane.

[00:19.0 --> 00:27.0]
Right grows the pane's width, Left shrinks it. The neighbors give and take flex weight as you go.

[00:27.0 --> 00:35.0]
Up and Down adjust height within the column. It's all flex-based, so the layout always stays proportional.

[00:35.0 --> 00:40.0]
Escape when it looks right. Arrow keys -- the simplest way to tune every pane's size.

